# camera: USB cameras (UVC). QEMU has none, so this checks the empty case;
# the descriptor parser and picture assembly are tested in beenet/src/uvc.rs.
$ camera
no camera (USB video class) plugged in; 'lsusb' lists the devices
$ camera raw
no camera plugged in
$ lsusb
~ xHCI|no USB controller
$ camera snap /me.jpg
camera: no camera plugged in ('lsusb' lists the devices)
$ camera record /me.avi 5
camera: no camera plugged in ('lsusb' lists the devices)
$ camera record /me.gif 5
usage: camera record FILE.avi SECONDS   (1 to 600; Ctrl+C stops early)
$ camera snap /me.jpg big
usage: camera snap FILE [WIDTHxHEIGHT]
$ camera watch /nowhere
camera watch: /nowhere: no such folder
$ camera watch / 0
usage: camera watch FOLDER [MINUTES]   (1 to 1440; Ctrl+C stops)
$ camera watch /
~ watching: a picture goes to / when something moves
camera: no camera plugged in ('lsusb' lists the devices)
~ watched for 0m 00s \(0 pictures\): 0 saved
$ camera timelapse /t.avi 0
usage: camera timelapse FILE.avi SECONDS [MINUTES]   (a picture every 1-3600 s, for up to a week; Ctrl+C stops)
$ camera timelapse /t.gif 5
usage: camera timelapse FILE.avi SECONDS [MINUTES]   (a picture every 1-3600 s, for up to a week; Ctrl+C stops)
$ camera timelapse /t.avi 5 60
~ a picture every 5 s into /t.avi
camera: no camera plugged in ('lsusb' lists the devices)
$ camera on
camera: no camera plugged in ('lsusb' lists the devices)
$ camera off
camera off
